      "message": "Did not commented on the previous note form pavankumar:\n\n   \"until now we treated  prefer_idle as bool (though it is int)\"\n\nbut I still don\u0027t get the reason for this change.\n\nWhichever we got for `prefere_idle` or `latency_sensitive` we are now using an *unsigned* value.\nNegative values are not supported and *0 only* means we are *not* prefere_idle/latency_sensitive.\n\nAm I missing something?\nOtherwise, I honestly find more generic and appropriate the check for \u0027\u003e0\u0027\n\nUnless pavankumar is asking for a signed type because he cares about negative values?\nBut the usage of negative values has never been officially supported by AOSP, does it?",
